  "source_review": [
    "The only changed previously-bound supporting file is frontend/package.json: Vite is pinned to 6.4.5 and vue-tsc to 3.3.14. The regenerated lock installs follow-redirects 1.16.2 and removes minimatch from the graph; official registry audit is zero. These build/type-tool changes do not alter the two reported Math.random test-username expressions, browser Cookie/CSRF handlers, Java authentication/transaction/cryptography code, or the Agent service-key boundary.",
    "Daily candidate selection now preserves explicit required/confirmed/protected POIs and uses the same typed candidate list for model input and validation. It does not add external endpoints, credentials, retrieval URLs or execution instructions. Request/model bounds and the existing route/time solver remain authoritative.",
    "The fact checklist derives display-only gaps from existing plan/input data. Vue text interpolation escapes source labels; staged facts still require explicit owner submission through the unchanged authenticated Java APIs. Source/confirmation/time checks remain on the server. The checklist never stamps a schedule feasible, confirmed or current.",
    "Proposal loading/confirm/discard move into a typed composable and still use the existing same-origin Axios client, CSRF headers, If-Match versions and server proposal dependency validation. Native export activation changes from hover to click; export sanitization and permission checks are unchanged.",
    "The four CI-only adapters are retired to historical evidence; their reviewed fixtures now run as tracked test sources. The excluded-day comparator retains strict JSON type/content/order comparison and only permits the two already-reviewed derived stale-reason representations when both sides are explicitly stale/unverified. Its negative cases now run in the backend suite.",
    "The new host inspector invokes Docker with an argument vector, check=True and a timeout, using only ps inventory and filesystem capacity reads. It does not invoke a shell, start services, install scheduling, change backup state or receive HTTP input. Its optional output is an explicitly supplied local CLI destination.",
    "The two new dependency regressions bind HTTP listeners only to loopback, use synthetic headers and a dedicated generated root containing a synthetic .env, and close their listeners. No application environment files, real credentials or external redirect targets are involved.",
    "All 22 primary query/path/region/severity/semantic-flow identities and their primary source bytes match the prior reviewed contexts. The 11 public capability GET callback overapproximations, validation marker GET, Cookie CSRF design, SQL version arithmetic, fixed-size server-generated TOTP plaintext, fixture-only PRNG, public-package chmod and bounded synthetic-admin status logging retain the same evidence and limitations."
  ],
  "prior_source_review": "docs/evidence/source-bound-review-20261030/codeql-source-review.json",
